Absolutely.
绝对的。

00:40:28.059 --> 00:40:29.059
Yeah.
对。

00:40:29.059 --> 00:40:30.059
I have a question.
我有个问题。

00:40:30.059 --> 00:40:39.239
I've already been, my mind's already been blown in these first two episodes about Barney in particular, I have the good fortune of a terrible memory.
在前两集里，我对巴尼的看法已经被颠覆了，我庆幸自己有着糟糕的记忆力。

00:40:39.239 --> 00:40:42.320
So I am watching this show almost new.
所以我几乎是像看新剧一样在看这部剧。

00:40:42.320 --> 00:40:45.280
I have forgotten quite a bit along the way.
一路上我已经忘得差不多了。

00:40:45.280 --> 00:40:52.199
And the idea of Barney being, I'm going to compare it as I will do several times to Eyes Wide Shut to Stanley Goodberg.
关于巴尼——我待会儿会像拿斯坦利·库布里克的《大开眼戒》作比较一样，多次提到这一点——

00:40:52.199 --> 00:40:59.559
So there's a scene at the end of Eyes Wide Shut where Sydney Pollock explains everything to Tom Cruise that just happened in this movie.
《大开眼戒》结尾处有一个场景，西德尼·波拉克向汤姆·克鲁斯解释了这部电影里刚刚发生的一切。

00:40:59.559 --> 00:41:03.239
People complained about this as you're just telling him, or at least the end.
人们抱怨说这纯粹是在直白地告诉观众，至少结尾是这样的。

00:41:03.239 --> 00:41:08.480
And it was years later that's a writer pointed out, you don't have to believe what he's saying.
直到多年后，才有一个编剧指出：你根本不用相信他说的话。

00:41:08.480 --> 00:41:14.360
Maybe he's lying the whole time, right, and that gives you a whole new, oh, right.
也许他从头到尾都在撒谎，对吧？这就带给你一个全新的视角，哦，原来如此。

00:41:14.360 --> 00:41:18.400
You've made a big assumption, but hold on, same thing with Barney.
你之前做了一个巨大的假设，但等等，巴尼也是这样。

00:41:18.400 --> 00:41:21.400
I think that, and maybe it's my bad memory.
我觉得，也许是因为我记性不好。

00:41:21.400 --> 00:41:33.654
The idea that he's making a lot of his stories up, or that he's not the Lothario and he hasn't been with that many women, is kind of new in my head right now and maybe I'm just forgetting things that I should have known.
他其实在瞎编很多自己的故事，或者他根本不是什么情圣，也没有和那么多女人交往过——这个概念现在对我来说挺新鲜的，也许我只是忘记了那些我本该知道的事情。

00:41:33.654 --> 00:41:39.949
When you were writing him, when you were first creating him, I know he's based on some some people that you knew.
当你在写这个角色，最初创造他的时候，我知道他是以你认识的一些人为原型的。

00:41:39.949 --> 00:41:41.453
What was the essence of it?
他的核心本质是什么？

00:41:41.453 --> 00:41:46.188
Was it, we need this kind of wild guy character who's going to all be about the hunt?
是我们需要这样一个满脑子只想着猎艳的狂野角色吗？

00:41:46.188 --> 00:41:50.700
Was it, we need a kind of broken soul who's covering it with with this adventure?
还是我们需要一个用这种冒险精神来掩饰自己破碎心灵的可怜虫？

00:41:50.700 --> 00:41:54.265
It was wanting to see the broken soul beneath toxic masculinity.
是为了展现有毒男子气概之下的破碎心灵。

00:41:54.265 --> 00:42:00.504
It was wanting to parody toxic masculinity and then humanize it by showing all over the broken parts underneath.
是为了讽刺有毒的男子气概，然后通过展示其下所有破碎的部分来使其人性化。

00:42:00.504 --> 00:42:02.454
And then you do nine seasons of it.
然后你一拍就是九季。

00:42:02.454 --> 00:42:10.809
And along the way, sometimes it just becomes like, let's do a funny joke about Bernie trying to get laid and you kind of lose some of that at moments.
而且有时候，整个过程就变成了，让我们开个关于巴尼想上床的滑稽玩笑吧，你有时就会忽略掉一些深度。

00:42:10.809 --> 00:42:17.160
But I think the through line for me and why why I don't look at it like, oh, we couldn't get away with that today.
但我认为对我来说贯穿始终的核心，以及为什么我不会觉得“哦，我们现在可拍不出那种东西了”。

00:42:17.160 --> 00:42:29.749
I it always at the intention was always let's show how broken this guy is underneath the suit and then show hints of him trying to grow and heal throughout the series and end him up somewhere different than he then he started.
我一直觉得，我们的初心始终是展现这个家伙西装革履之下的破碎感，然后展现他在整部剧里试图成长和治愈的蛛丝马迹，最终让他走向一个与起点不同的结局。

00:42:29.749 --> 00:42:41.280
And I also think whatever whether you're a guy who's obsessed with getting laid and meeting women and not that successful at it or you're part of like pick up culture and you actually are successful with it.
而且我也觉得，不管你是一个满脑子只想上床、结识女性却又不太成功的家伙，还是你属于搭讪文化的一员并且实际上真的很成功。

00:42:41.280 --> 00:42:44.280
Both of them carry a lot of pain underneath them.
他们两者内心深处都承载着极大的痛苦。

00:42:44.280 --> 00:42:45.280
They do.
确实如此。

00:42:45.280 --> 00:42:57.239
You don't behave that way single-mindedly and almost psychotically if you're not feeling some sort of great absence at the center of your heart.
如果你不是在内心最深处感受到某种巨大的空虚，你是不会那么专一甚至近乎疯狂地做出那种行为的。

00:42:57.239 --> 00:42:58.239
I know.
我懂。

00:42:58.239 --> 00:42:59.239
For 100%.
百分之百。

00:42:59.239 --> 00:42:59.802
addiction.
就像上瘾一样。

00:42:59.802 --> 00:43:01.210
It's like filling a hole.
这就好比在填补一个洞。

00:43:01.210 --> 00:43:03.800
It really is like a missing piece in somebody.
真的就像是某人身上缺失的一块。

00:43:03.800 --> 00:43:04.300
Yeah.
是啊。

00:43:04.300 --> 00:43:05.752
That's how I look at Barney.
这就是我怎么看巴尼的。

00:43:05.752 --> 00:43:13.640
And that's why I have such, I've on him so endearing in these early episodes because I see that spark, I see that initial idea in him in these episodes.
这也是为什么我对他在前几集里感到如此喜爱，因为我在这些剧集里看到了那种火花，看到了他最初的那个构想。

00:43:13.400 --> 00:43:22.460
Well, one of the fascinating, I think kind of tensions in the show is I think you and Carter would say, no, we always saw him as kind of sad and broken but trying.
嗯，我觉得剧里一种很迷人的张力在于，你和卡特大概会说：“不，我们一直觉得他挺悲惨、挺破碎，但他一直在努力。”

00:43:22.460 --> 00:43:25.518
And he doesn't get laid nearly as much as he claims to.
而且他并没有像自己吹嘘的那样频频上床。

00:43:25.518 --> 00:43:28.019
Whereas I think Neil would disagree with you.
然而我想尼尔可能会不同意你们的看法。

00:43:28.019 --> 00:43:32.244
I think Neil thought, Neil played him as if he was getting late every night.
我觉得尼尔认为，尼尔对这个角色的演绎就好像他每晚都在上床一样。

00:43:32.244 --> 00:43:32.744
Yeah.
对。

00:43:32.744 --> 00:43:33.244
Yeah.
对。

00:43:33.244 --> 00:43:37.246
I mean, I think that's some of the interesting tension of the character.
我是说，我觉得这正是这个角色一些有趣张力的来源。

00:43:37.246 --> 00:43:41.137
Well, it's funny because Neil, I mean, it was like a superhero outfit.
嗯，这很有趣，因为尼尔，我的意思是，这就像是一套超级英雄制服。

00:43:41.137 --> 00:43:43.194
Neil had to put on every week, right?
尼尔每周都得穿上它，对吧？

00:43:43.194 --> 00:43:43.972
It was Batman.
就像蝙蝠侠。

00:43:43.972 --> 00:43:44.862
It was Iron Man.
就像钢铁侠。

00:43:44.862 --> 00:43:49.809
He had to put this on and be that superhero and perform that and believe his own stories.
他必须穿上这身行头，当那个超级英雄，完成表演，并相信他自己编的故事。

00:43:49.809 --> 00:43:59.204
And then those moments where we did have him step out of that and show some other side, they were very effective because of how much he had committed to the first thing.
然后，每当我们需要他跳出这种状态、展现出另一面时，这些时刻由于他之前对前者的极度投入，而显得非常奏效。

00:43:58.760 --> 00:44:06.599
And I always found myself more jealous of the other characters, because I thought they all had costumes that I wasn't allowed to wear.
而且我发现自己总是更嫉妒其他角色，因为我觉得他们都有我不能穿的戏服。

00:44:06.599 --> 00:44:19.280
Yeah, like I thought they all had some armor up around them that allowed them to, I don't know, float through the world of how I met your mother in a less just vulnerable way.
对，就像我觉得他们都在自己周围穿上了一层盔甲，让他们能够，我不知道，用一种没那么脆弱的方式在《老爸老妈的浪漫史》的世界里游荡。

00:44:19.280 --> 00:44:26.519
I mean, everyone had their vulnerable moments to be sure I'm not taking that away from anyone, but Ted just, he didn't have that armor.
我的意思是，每个人都有脆弱的时刻，这是肯定的，我不是在否定这一点，但泰德就是，他没有那层盔甲。

00:44:26.519 --> 00:44:30.960
I had to kind of have my nerve endings exposed for nine years.
我有九年的时间都得让自己的神经末梢暴露在外。

00:44:30.960 --> 00:44:38.400
Yeah, you were on your own a lot of the time because Marshall had Lily and that meant sort of Siegel had handing into bond with.
对，你大部分时间都是孤身一人，因为马修有莉莉，这意味着某种程度上杰森有可以依靠的伴侣。

00:44:38.400 --> 00:44:39.840
Robin was supposed to be this thing.
罗宾本该是这样一个存在。

